========================================================================
  9. WALL-SUN-SUN PRIMES AND F_{p-(p|5)} mod p^2
========================================================================

A Wall-Sun-Sun prime p satisfies p^2 | F_{p - (p|5)}.
(p|5) is the Legendre symbol (p/5).
No Wall-Sun-Sun primes are known. Testing our primes:

  p=2: special (p=2)
  p=  3: (p|5)=-1, F_  4 mod 3^2 = F_4 mod     9 =     3  
  p=5: special (p=5, (p|5)=0)
  p=  7: (p|5)=-1, F_  8 mod 7^2 = F_8 mod    49 =    21  
  p= 11: (p|5)=+1, F_ 10 mod 11^2 = F_10 mod   121 =    55  
  p= 13: (p|5)=-1, F_ 14 mod 13^2 = F_14 mod   169 =    39  
  p= 17: (p|5)=-1, F_ 18 mod 17^2 = F_18 mod   289 =   272  
  p= 19: (p|5)=+1, F_ 18 mod 19^2 = F_18 mod   361 =    57  
  p= 23: (p|5)=-1, F_ 24 mod 23^2 = F_24 mod   529 =   345  
  p= 29: (p|5)=+1, F_ 28 mod 29^2 = F_28 mod   841 =   754  
  p= 31: (p|5)=+1, F_ 30 mod 31^2 = F_30 mod   961 =   775  
  p= 37: (p|5)=-1, F_ 38 mod 37^2 = F_38 mod  1369 =   481  
  p= 41: (p|5)=+1, F_ 40 mod 41^2 = F_40 mod  1681 =  1599  
  p= 43: (p|5)=-1, F_ 44 mod 43^2 = F_44 mod  1849 =  1677  
  p= 47: (p|5)=-1, F_ 48 mod 47^2 = F_48 mod  2209 =   752  
  p= 53: (p|5)=-1, F_ 54 mod 53^2 = F_54 mod  2809 =  1484  
  p= 59: (p|5)=+1, F_ 58 mod 59^2 = F_58 mod  3481 =   590  
  p= 61: (p|5)=+1, F_ 60 mod 61^2 = F_60 mod  3721 =  2928  
  p= 67: (p|5)=-1, F_ 68 mod 67^2 = F_68 mod  4489 =   469  
  p= 71: (p|5)=+1, F_ 70 mod 71^2 = F_70 mod  5041 =  3905  
  p= 73: (p|5)=-1, F_ 74 mod 73^2 = F_74 mod  5329 =  4234  
  p= 79: (p|5)=+1, F_ 78 mod 79^2 = F_78 mod  6241 =  3871  
  p= 83: (p|5)=-1, F_ 84 mod 83^2 = F_84 mod  6889 =  1743  
  p= 89: (p|5)=+1, F_ 88 mod 89^2 = F_88 mod  7921 =   445  
  p= 97: (p|5)=-1, F_ 98 mod 97^2 = F_98 mod  9409 =  3589  

No Wall-Sun-Sun primes found up to p=97 (none known at all).
Connection to our framework: a Wall-Sun-Sun prime would create an
exceptionally strong Fibonacci divisibility, but none exist among our primes.

========================================================================
  10. FIBONACCI/LUCAS AT AND AROUND FUNDAMENTAL PRIMES
========================================================================

For each prime p, compute F_p, F_{p-1}, F_{p+1}, L_p and factor:

  p = 2:
    F_ 1 =            1 = 1
    F_ 2  =            1 = 1
    F_ 3 =            2 = 2
    L_ 2  =            3 = 3
    (p|5) = 1, p | F_{p-(p|5)} = p | F_1: False

  p = 3:
    F_ 2 =            1 = 1
    F_ 3  =            2 = 2
    F_ 4 =            3 = 3
    L_ 3  =            4 = 2^2
    (p|5) = -1, p | F_{p-(p|5)} = p | F_4: True

  p = 5:
    F_ 4 =            3 = 3
    F_ 5  =            5 = 5
    F_ 6 =            8 = 2^3
    L_ 5  =           11 = 11
    (p|5) = 0, p | F_{p-(p|5)} = p | F_5: True

  p = 7:
    F_ 6 =            8 = 2^3
    F_ 7  =           13 = 13
    F_ 8 =           21 = 3 * 7
    L_ 7  =           29 = 29
    (p|5) = -1, p | F_{p-(p|5)} = p | F_8: True

  p = 11:
    F_10 =           55 = 5 * 11
    F_11  =           89 = 89
    F_12 =          144 = 2^4 * 3^2
    L_11  =          199 = 199
    (p|5) = 1, p | F_{p-(p|5)} = p | F_10: True

  p = 13:
    F_12 =          144 = 2^4 * 3^2
    F_13  =          233 = 233
    F_14 =          377 = 13 * 29
    L_13  =          521 = 521
    (p|5) = -1, p | F_{p-(p|5)} = p | F_14: True

  p = 17:
    F_16 =          987 = 3 * 7 * 47
    F_17  =         1597 = 1597
    F_18 =         2584 = 2^3 * 17 * 19
    L_17  =         3571 = 3571
    (p|5) = -1, p | F_{p-(p|5)} = p | F_18: True

  p = 19:
    F_18 =         2584 = 2^3 * 17 * 19
    F_19  =         4181 = 37 * 113
    F_20 =         6765 = 3 * 5 * 11 * 41
    L_19  =         9349 = 9349
    (p|5) = 1, p | F_{p-(p|5)} = p | F_18: True

  p = 23:
    F_22 =        17711 = 89 * 199
    F_23  =        28657 = 28657
    F_24 =        46368 = 2^5 * 3^2 * 7 * 23
    L_23  =        64079 = 139 * 461
    (p|5) = -1, p | F_{p-(p|5)} = p | F_24: True

  p = 29:
    F_28 =       317811 = 3 * 13 * 29 * 281
    F_29  =       514229 = 514229
    F_30 =       832040 = 2^3 * 5 * 11 * 31 * 61
    L_29  =      1149851 = 59 * 19489
    (p|5) = 1, p | F_{p-(p|5)} = p | F_28: True

  p = 31:
    F_30 =       832040 = 2^3 * 5 * 11 * 31 * 61
    F_31  =      1346269 = 557 * 2417
    F_32 =      2178309 = 3 * 7 * 47 * 2207
    L_31  =      3010349 = 3010349
    (p|5) = 1, p | F_{p-(p|5)} = p | F_30: True


--- Pattern analysis ---

Known: for prime p != 5, p | F_{p - (p/5)}
  p=2: 2|F_3=2 YES
  p=3: 3|F_4=3 YES (3 = +2 mod 5, so (3|5)=-1, F_{3-(-1)}=F_4=3)

Factoring F_p for fundamental primes:
  F_2 = 1 (trivial)
  F_3 = 2 (prime)
  F_5 = 5 (prime, = p itself!)
  F_7 = 13 (prime)
  F_11 = 89 (prime)
  F_13 = 233 (prime)

ALL F_p for our fundamental primes are themselves prime!
This is because: if p is prime, then F_p is a 'Fibonacci prime candidate'.
Known result: if F_n is prime and n > 4, then n is prime.
(Converse fails: F_19 = 4181 = 37*113 is composite despite 19 being prime.)
  F_19 = 4181 = 37 * 113

Is F_p prime for each prime p?
  F_ 2 =            1  composite = 1
  F_ 3 =            2  PRIME
  F_ 5 =            5  PRIME
  F_ 7 =           13  PRIME
