  F_23 =        28657  PRIME
  F_29 =       514229  PRIME
  F_31 =      1346269  composite = 557 * 2417
  F_37 =     24157817  composite = 73 * 149 * 2221
  F_41 =    165580141  composite = 2789 * 59369
  F_43 =    433494437  PRIME
  F_47 =   2971215073  PRIME

========================================================================
  11. PYTHAGOREAN-TYPE IDENTITY: F_{n+1}^2 + F_n^2 = F_{2n+1}
========================================================================

Verification and exploration of F_{n+1}^2 + F_n^2 = F_{2n+1}:

  n= 0: F_1^2 + F_0^2 = 1^2 + 0^2 = 1 + 0 = 1 = F_1 = 1 [OK]
  n= 1: F_2^2 + F_1^2 = 1^2 + 1^2 = 1 + 1 = 2 = F_3 = 2 [OK]
  n= 2: F_3^2 + F_2^2 = 2^2 + 1^2 = 4 + 1 = 5 = F_5 = 5 [OK]
  n= 3: F_4^2 + F_3^2 = 3^2 + 2^2 = 9 + 4 = 13 = F_7 = 13 [OK]
  n= 4: F_5^2 + F_4^2 = 5^2 + 3^2 = 25 + 9 = 34 = F_9 = 34 [OK]
  n= 5: F_6^2 + F_5^2 = 8^2 + 5^2 = 64 + 25 = 89 = F_11 = 89 [OK]
  n= 6: F_7^2 + F_6^2 = 13^2 + 8^2 = 169 + 64 = 233 = F_13 = 233 [OK]
  n= 7: F_8^2 + F_7^2 = 21^2 + 13^2 = 441 + 169 = 610 = F_15 = 610 [OK]
  n= 8: F_9^2 + F_8^2 = 34^2 + 21^2 = 1156 + 441 = 1597 = F_17 = 1597 [OK]
  n= 9: F_10^2 + F_9^2 = 55^2 + 34^2 = 3025 + 1156 = 4181 = F_19 = 4181 [OK]
  n=10: F_11^2 + F_10^2 = 89^2 + 55^2 = 7921 + 3025 = 10946 = F_21 = 10946 [OK]
  n=11: F_12^2 + F_11^2 = 144^2 + 89^2 = 20736 + 7921 = 28657 = F_23 = 28657 [OK]

--- Special cases at n=3 and n=7 ---

n=3: F_4^2 + F_3^2 = 3^2 + 2^2 = 9 + 4 = 13 = F_7
  F_7 = 13 = 13 (prime!)
  13 = sum of squares of consecutive Fibonacci primes (2,3)
  13 is itself a Fibonacci prime

n=7: F_8^2 + F_7^2 = 21^2 + 13^2 = 441 + 169 = 610 = F_15
  F_15 = 610 = 2 * 5 * 61
  610 = 2 * 5 * 61
  So (forbidden number)^2 + 13^2 = 2 * 5 * 61 = F_15
  Note: 61 is prime, and 2*5 = 10 = product of fundamental primes

n=4: F_5^2 + F_4^2 = 5^2 + 3^2 = 25 + 9 = 34 = F_9
  F_9 = 34 = 2 * 17

Related identity: F_{n+1}^2 - F_n^2 = F_{n-1}*F_{n+2}
  n=1: F_2^2 - F_1^2 = 0, F_0*F_3 = 0, match=True
  n=2: F_3^2 - F_2^2 = 3, F_1*F_4 = 3, match=True
  n=3: F_4^2 - F_3^2 = 5, F_2*F_5 = 5, match=True
  n=4: F_5^2 - F_4^2 = 16, F_3*F_6 = 16, match=True
  n=5: F_6^2 - F_5^2 = 39, F_4*F_7 = 39, match=True
  n=6: F_7^2 - F_6^2 = 105, F_5*F_8 = 105, match=True
  n=7: F_8^2 - F_7^2 = 272, F_6*F_9 = 272, match=True
  n=8: F_9^2 - F_8^2 = 715, F_7*F_10 = 715, match=True
  n=9: F_10^2 - F_9^2 = 1869, F_8*F_11 = 1869, match=True

Cassini's identity: F_{n+1}*F_{n-1} - F_n^2 = (-1)^n
  n= 1: F_2*F_0 - F_n^2 = -1 = (-1)^1 = -1
  n= 2: F_3*F_1 - F_n^2 = 1 = (-1)^2 = 1
  n= 3: F_4*F_2 - F_n^2 = -1 = (-1)^3 = -1
  n= 4: F_5*F_3 - F_n^2 = 1 = (-1)^4 = 1
  n= 5: F_6*F_4 - F_n^2 = -1 = (-1)^5 = -1
  n= 6: F_7*F_5 - F_n^2 = 1 = (-1)^6 = 1
  n= 7: F_8*F_6 - F_n^2 = -1 = (-1)^7 = -1
  n= 8: F_9*F_7 - F_n^2 = 1 = (-1)^8 = 1
  n= 9: F_10*F_8 - F_n^2 = -1 = (-1)^9 = -1
  n=10: F_11*F_9 - F_n^2 = 1 = (-1)^10 = 1
  n=11: F_12*F_10 - F_n^2 = -1 = (-1)^11 = -1

========================================================================
  12. QR COUNTS OF FUNDAMENTAL PRIMES = FIBONACCI SEQUENCE
========================================================================

For prime p, the number of quadratic residues mod p (excluding 0) is (p-1)/2.

  p= 3: QR count = (p-1)/2 = 1 = F_1
  p= 5: QR count = (p-1)/2 = 2 = F_3
  p= 7: QR count = (p-1)/2 = 3 = F_4
  p=11: QR count = (p-1)/2 = 5 = F_5
  p=13: QR count = (p-1)/2 = 6
  p=17: QR count = (p-1)/2 = 8 = F_6
  p=19: QR count = (p-1)/2 = 9
  p=23: QR count = (p-1)/2 = 11
  p=29: QR count = (p-1)/2 = 14
  p=31: QR count = (p-1)/2 = 15

The QR counts for {3, 5, 7, 11} are {1, 2, 3, 5} = {F_1, F_3, F_4, F_5}
This is NOT consecutive Fibonacci! The Fibonacci numbers are:
  F_0=0, F_1=1, F_2=1, F_3=2, F_4=3, F_5=5, F_6=8, ...
The QR counts 1, 2, 3, 5 correspond to indices 1 (or 2), 3, 4, 5

But notice: (p-1)/2 for p = 3,5,7,11 gives 1,2,3,5
The GAPS are: 1, 1, 2 (between 1-2, 2-3, 3-5)
These gaps are themselves 1, 1, 2 = beginning of Fibonacci!

Continuation: p=13 gives QR=6 (not Fibonacci)
  F_5=5, F_6=8. So 6 is NOT Fibonacci. The pattern breaks at p=13.

Alternative interpretation: QR counts as function of PRIME INDEX:
  pi(3)=2nd prime: QR=1
  pi(5)=3rd prime: QR=2
  pi(7)=4th prime: QR=3
  pi(11)=5th prime: QR=5
  pi(13)=6th prime: QR=6 (not Fibonacci)
  pi(17)=7th prime: QR=8 = F_6!
  Verify: QR(17) = (17-1)/2 = 8
  So F_6 = 8 reappears at p=17!

Checking: (p-1)/2 = F_k for some k?
  p=  3: QR=   1 = F_1 [FIBONACCI]
  p=  5: QR=   2 = F_3 [FIBONACCI]
  p=  7: QR=   3 = F_4 [FIBONACCI]
  p= 11: QR=   5 = F_5 [FIBONACCI]
  p= 13: QR=   6 (not Fibonacci)
